Fix NULL focus_surface dereference in touch_can_grab_surface

meta_wayland_touch_cancel() clears focus_surface on all touch infos
without removing them from the touches table, so entries with a NULL
focus_surface are legal. When a client then issues xdg_toplevel.resize
with a matching slot serial, meta_wayland_touch_find_grab_sequence()
dereferences the NULL focus_surface in touch_can_grab_surface(),
crashing gnome-shell with SIGSEGV.

--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
@@ -656,6 +656,9 @@
 {
   MetaWaylandSurface *subsurface;
 
+  if (!touch_info->focus_surface)
+    return FALSE;
+
   if (touch_info->focus_surface->surface == surface)
     return TRUE;
 
